FILED s522b (Opus, 2026-10-19) from member 0's (#1570) probes.  PRE-EXISTING (identical on aff112d7).

    package A1; sub w { "A1" } package B1; our @ISA = ("A1"); package C1; our @ISA=("A1"); sub w { "C1" }
    package D; use mro "c3"; our @ISA = ("B1","C1"); package main; print D->w, "\n";

perl 5.40.3: C1 (C3: D B1 C1 A1).  PCL: A1.  `mro::get_linear_isa("D")` answers the C3 list D,B1,C1,A1 but dispatch disagrees: %pcl-dispatch-method takes the CLOS class-precedence-list only when @ISA is EMPTY and otherwise walks @ISA depth-first.  Without the pragma perl's default is DFS (A1) and PCL agrees by accident.  docs/not-supported.md "mro pragma" says PCL ALWAYS uses C3 -- not true for this path; fix the doc or the dispatch (the walk should honour the class's mro, and the CLOS CPL is C3).  Probes: scratch/s522b/p/r9b.pl r9c.pl.
